  "notes": "Gold11 CG84C8FA12D2 (corpus/01_10839000, 10839000_01_full_scan.ply, sc_71cf0b216f43) parallel AI relabel (gold11_audit, 2026-10-17); human gold untouched. Conventions: apex locus (outer-skin arc midline, outer-skin patch pairs), small formed bends count, joggles = 2 bends, interrupted collinear folds = one line. Part: closed rectangular C-section frame ~312 x 206 x 40 mm: flat bottom frame ring (patches 1/2) with 4 walls folded up from it (long 3, 4; short 7, 8); each short wall ends in a 12 mm inward lip (lip ring 5 top / 6 underside) that exists only between the long top flanges' free edges (~133 mm, corner zones are a cut wall edge under the long flange, no fold); each long wall ends in a 35 mm inward top flange (9/12, 10/11) with a ~1.9 mm joggle ~22 mm in from the wall (~48 deg web: patch 14 on the wall-3 side, plane-fitted web skins on the wall-4 side). 12 formed bends = 8 wall folds (human M01-M08, re-placed on the outer apex) + 4 joggle bends (2 per long-side top flange, missing in human gold); STEP cad_v10_count = 12. Wall-3 joggle bend B: its lower (convex) web skin is not scanned, so that line sits on the scanned upper-skin (concave) arc, ~1.5 mm from the convex apex. Extents: auto where it matched the scanned outer arc; overrides (M01-M05, M07, joggle B wall-4) set to the scanned outer-arc ends (analysis/verify_lines.py). Prep run once for this audit (none existed); iterations run1/run2 kept; this final run = run2 geometry with final notes.",
